@startuml context-diagram
title WildTrack RAD – System Context

top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<subsystem>> #EAF2F8
  BorderColor<<subsystem>> #1F4E79
  BackgroundColor<<external system>> #F4F4F4
  BorderColor<<external system>> #666666
}

' ---------- People (user interactions, not interface-table entries) ----------
actor "Field Ranger" as Ranger
actor "Supervisor" as Supervisor
actor "Law Enforcement Liaison" as Liaison
actor "System Administrator" as Admin
actor "Rehabilitation Veterinarian" as Vet
actor "Partner Recipient\n(police/sheriff, U.S. Fish & Wildlife,\nland manager)" as Partner

rectangle "Email / notification service" <<external system>> as Email

' ---------- System boundary ----------
rectangle "WildTrack RAD  (system boundary)" as WT {
  rectangle "iPad app\n(authoring, offline drafts,\nqueued notices)" <<subsystem>> as App
  rectangle "WildTrack server\n(workflow, redaction policy,\naudit log, partner web view)" <<subsystem>> as Server
}

' ---------- External systems ----------
rectangle "State-issued iPad\n(hardware + iPadOS, MDM)" <<external system>> as IPad
rectangle "State SSO" <<external system>> as SSO
rectangle "Biologist-maintained\nsensitive species list\n(source/format TBD)" <<external system>> as Species
rectangle "PDF renderer\n(internal vs third-party TBD)" <<external system>> as PDF

' ---------- User interactions ----------
Ranger --> App : create/edit reports, drafts,\nphotos, urgent notice
Supervisor --> Server : review queue, approve/reject,\nselect recipients, exceptions, delegation
Liaison --> Server : secondary review\nand decision
Admin --> Server : manage users, roles,\ntemplates, species rules

' ---------- Platform ----------
App ..> IPad : runs on\n(local encrypted storage)

' ---------- Interfaces (numbering matches the spec's External Interfaces table) ----------
App <--> Server : IF-02 (internal): report/photo sync,\nqueued notices, sync state
Server <--> SSO : IF-01: login request,\nidentity and role/group claims
Server --> Email : IF-03: partner links/codes,\nranger and reviewer alerts, urgent notices
Email --> Ranger : IF-03 delivery: status,\nrejection/change notices
Email --> Supervisor : IF-03 delivery:\naction alerts
Email --> Liaison : IF-03 delivery:\naction alerts
Email --> Vet : IF-03 delivery: minimal urgent notice\n(species, condition, pickup location)
Partner <--> Server : IF-04 partner web view: code,\nauthorized report, PDF, receipt
Species --> Server : IF-05: species identifiers,\nsensitivity, effective date
Server --> PDF : IF-06: redacted report fields,\nrecipient name, download time
PDF --> Server : IF-06: generated PDF

note bottom of WT
  Boundary decision: the iPad app and the server are both part of WildTrack,
  so IF-02 is an INTERNAL interface between subsystems. The iPad hardware,
  iPadOS and MDM are external platform dependencies owned by State IT.
  Only system-to-system connections are interface-table entries;
  actor links show user interactions.
end note

@enduml
